\par\plain {The new sensors used a protein which was more like a Venus flytrap with brains than an antibody\loch\af0\hich\af0\dbch\af0\uc1\u8217\'92s passive, single-purpose template. \u8220\'93Assayin\u8221\'94 in its receptive state was a long, bell-shaped molecule, a tube opening out into a broad funnel. This conformation was metastable; the charge distribution on the molecule rendered it exquisitely sensitive, spring-loaded. Anything large enough colliding with the inner surface of the funnel caused a lightning-fast wave of deformation, engulfing and shrink-wrapping the intruder. The microprocessor, noting the sprung trap, could then probe the captive molecule by searching for a shape of the assayin which imprisoned it even more snugly. There were no more wasted, mismatched collisions-no more insulin molecules striking cholesterol antibodies, yielding no information at all. Assayin always knew what had hit it.}
